==================================================
1. CRITICAL PROJECT IDENTITY
==================================================

PRODUCT NAME:
PatchPilot

TAGLINE:
"Verify the fix. Ship with confidence."

CORE PRODUCT PROMISE:
PatchPilot helps developers resolve software errors efficiently by checking whether AI-generated technical advice is accurate and up to date before proposing code changes.

The product combines two major capabilities:

1. A token-efficient AI coding agent.
2. A stale-answer verification engine.

Both capabilities must operate as parts of ONE integrated product.

COMPETITION CONTEXT:

We are addressing two Global AI Hackathon problem statements:

BIFROST:
"Build a Coding Agent That Gets the Job Done on the Fewest Tokens"

TAVILY:
"Build a Stale-Answer Detector for AI Applications"

The future backend must demonstrate meaningful functionality for BOTH challenges.

The coding agent must eventually:
- Diagnose real programming errors.
- Work on narrowly scoped development tasks.
- Minimize unnecessary model tokens.
- Use budget controls.
- Support model fallback.
- Require human approval before dangerous actions.
- Produce small, reviewable code changes.
- Execute controlled tests.
- Report real token and cost usage.

The verification engine must eventually:
- Analyze AI-generated answers.
- Extract factual claims.
- Identify claims potentially affected by changing information.
- Verify claims using current sources.
- Distinguish verified, outdated, and uncertain claims.
- Provide claim-specific evidence and corrections.

The coding workflow will use the verification engine internally.

IMPORTANT:
This initial implementation is FRONTEND ONLY.

Create a fully interactive frontend using clearly labeled local demo data.

Do not connect external services yet.

